# Observed oracle for PA-08-F66 / inc-tek.8.8: the Horn of the Kobolds, blown by
# a NON-kobold wielder, must summon HOSTILE kobolds. The default chargen makes an
# orc barbarian (a non-kobold), so no race-setting is needed. Read by
# check_kobold_horn.sh, which examines the summoned kobold's Hostility section.
#
# Pre-fix (HEAD): the declarative EA_SUMMON always summoned FRIENDLY, so the
# kobold feels allegiance/neutrality toward the blower. Post-fix: the new
# On Event EV_MAGIC_HIT handler makes a non-kobold wielder's kobolds HOSTILE, so
# the kobold feels enmity toward the blower.
#
# Navigation modelled on horn-panic.keys (bd inc-j4dy): wizard mode entered once
# with 'w' 'y'; Item Acquisition RIGHT*28 reaches Horns; the candidate list
# highlights the middle of three rows, so @until stops on the row after the one
# wanted; 'Enter Item Level:' sets the item plus; 's' stows the item.
@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN
SPACE                   # Auto-Identify Items
DOWN*9
SPACE                   # Freeze Monsters
ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*28                # Horns
@until "Horn of the Kobolds" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
3
ENTER
s
ESC

a
@dump:activate-menu
a
@dump:blown

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@until "kobold (class" RIGHT
DOWN*40
@dump:kobold-after
ESC
@quit
